The attached image (Fig. 5) demonstrates that Nano-11 enhances the uptake of adsorbed antigens by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs). Panel A, through flow cytometry dot plots, shows a significant increase in cells positive for both Nano-11 and OVA when the antigen is adsorbed to the nanoparticles. Panel B, a histogram of FITC-OVA fluorescence, quantifies this by showing a pronounced shift in cell count to higher fluorescence intensities for Nano-11+OVA compared to soluble OVA or Nano-11 alone. These findings indicate that Nano-11 effectively delivers negatively charged antigens to DCs, a critical step for its adjuvant function.